The close's margin list says that, apart from the six purge misses and commitTwoTokensTurns (8.95), 'No other case is above 8.5', and gives the keep form at 8.32. My release re-measures on d88bdb1, all at 1-minute loads of 10 or less, put three more cases above 8.5 ms best:
- userSharedApplyTurns(.keep): 9.04 ms ([9.04, 9.36, 9.24], load 3.01-3.11, bench-rerun-edge) and 8.50 ms ([8.85, 8.50, 8.51], load about 4.2-4.4, bench-run2);
- divergenceTurns 'on to fresh contents': 8.83 ([8.83, 10.39, 9.00], load about 4.2-4.4) and 8.35 (load 3.0);
- concentrationCommitRerouteTurns ('a commit that re-routes the ids moved away'): 8.71 ([10.61, 8.71, 8.74], load 4.57) and 8.05 (load 3.0).
All of them pass (best of 3 at or under 10 ms), so there is no new FAIL cause today. But keep-form sits as near the limit as commitTwoTokensTurns, which measured 9.27 at load 3.67 in my re-run. Against the fixer's close log at similar loads, my figures were up to about 17% higher: divergenceTurns 7.55 there against 8.35-8.83 here, concentrationCommitRerouteTurns 7.47 against 8.05-8.71. A later --perf or Stage 5 --full on this host could therefore see a new red case, which point 3 would have to take to the owner.
